00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.270 align:start position:0%
 
reach  mr speaker this new blueprint delivers  three  high-speed lines first that's crew to  manchester second birmingham to the east  midlands with hs2 trains continuing to  central nottingham and central derby  chesterfield and sheffield on an  upgraded main line and third a brand new  high-speed line from warrington to  manchester and to the western border of  yorkshire slashing journey times across  the north  mr speaker  mr speaker  well  mr figger i know they'll want to hear  the detail  of those journey times and they'll also  want to explain  why their constituents would wish to  wait  would wish to wait decades more to  deliver a journey almost no faster at  all than these plans today so mr speaker  i've heard some people say uh that we're  we're just going about and this is i  think their point electrifying uh the  transpanine route this is wrong what  we're actually doing is investing 23  billion pounds to deliver northern  powerhouse rail and the transparent  route upgrade unlocking east-west travel  across the north of england so in total  this package is 110 miles of new  high-speed line  all of it in the midlands and the north  it's 180 miles of newly electrified line  all of it in the midlands and the north  i just remember reminding the honourable  gentleman of their 63 miles of  electrified line in 13 years  uh we'll upgrade the east coast mainline  with a package of investment on track  improvements and digital signaling  bringing down journey times between  london leeds darlington newcastle and  edinburgh bringing benefits to the  northeast much much sooner than under  the previous plans and it adds capacity  and speeds of services  over more than 400 miles of lines the  vast majority of it in the midlands and  the north  we'll study how best to take hs2 trains  into leeds as well and we'll start work  on the new west yorkshire mass transit  system  righting the wrong  of this major city probably the largest  in europe which doesn't have a mass  transit system we commit today to  supporting west yorkshire combined  authority over the long term to ensure  that this time it actually gets done  in short mr speaker we're about to  embark on one of the biggest single acts  of leveling up of any government in  history  well listen to the numbers well listen  to the numbers it's five times more than  was spent on crossrail it's ten times  more than was spent on delivering the  olympics but they still think it's a  small package mr speaker  it will achieve the same similar or  faster journey times to london and on  the core northern powerhouse network  than the original proposals and will  bring the benefits years earlier as we  double in some case cases triple the  capacity so let me just set out a few of  these investments  rail journeys between birmingham and  nottingham cut from an hour and a  quarter to 26 minutes city centre to  city centre journeys between york and  manchester down to 55 minutes from 83  minutes today commuters will be able to  get from bradford to leeds in just 12  minutes almost half the time it takes  today there'll be earlier benefits for  places like sheffield and chesterfield  trips from newcastle to birmingham will  be slashed by almost 30 minutes and  passengers in durham and darlington will  benefit from smoother more reliable  trains as the irp delivers not just for  our largest cities but also for smaller  places and towns for example kettering  market harbor leicester loughborough  grantham newark redford doncaster  wakefield gooseberry  huddersfield staley bridge they could  all see improvements electrification  faster services benefiting  in ways that they would not have done  under the original hs2 program mr  speaker we're not stopping there today's  plan is about those places which connect  and interact with hs2 and northern  powerhouse rail so the scale of ambition  with many of these projects uh lying  outside of the scope so just yesterday i  opened the first beaching reversal uh  reversing the beaching axe uh and we are  going to be doing the same in  northumberland from washington blithe  newcastle line and many others we're  investing 2 billion in cycling water  walking 3 billion  in turn up and go bus services and tens  of billions in our country's roads so mr  speaker after decades of decline with  constrained capacity and poor  reliability finally this plan will give  passengers and the north and the  midlands the service they need and they  deserve it's not just about  infrastructure we're going to make train  travel much easier as well today i can  confirm 360 million pounds to reform  fares and ticketing with a roll out of  contactless pay-as-you-go ticketing to  700 urban stations including 400 in the  north mr speaker is a landmark plan far  by far by far the biggest  of any network improvement and focused  on the north and midlands with more  seats more frequent services shorter  journeys it meets the needs of today's  passengers and the future generations  and we're getting started immediately

